tents","complete project","Project source",[185],{"_51":186,"_26":158,"_179":187},"Open the complete exploration project","GPL-3.0 source with complete index.html, vendored Three.js, procedural textures, and implementation notes. Run python3 -m http.server 5191 and open localhost:5191/index.html; file:// loading is unsupported. The original author has ended active development. The creator describes an exploration prototype, not a finished campaign; no complete win/loss loop is claimed.","Access type","playable","Play or run",[192],{"_51":193,"_26":194,"_179":195},"Explore Sakura Crossing","https://danymaniglie-cmyk.github.io/3d-sakura-crossing/","Exploration prototype. WASD walks, Shift runs, mouse drag looks, E talks, F enters/exits the car, and Space/C swims up/down. Touch controls included; mobile performance remains limited.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[203],{"_51":204,"_26":205,"_179":-7},"Read the rendering and implementation recipe","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing/blob/main/CARTOON.md","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[210,211,212,213],"Explore the browser world on foot, then try the car, river, and moving bridge.","Read the credits and the author’s account of using a local Qwen model through Claude Code CLI.","Inspect CARTOON.md and the complete index.html plus vendored Three.js dependency.","Serve a local copy over HTTP, change one interaction, and verify movement and collisions.","AI workflow / foundation context","The repository credits code generation to locally running Qwen 3.8 27B, followed by human review, debugging, and extensions. In the linked build account the author identifies Claude Code CLI as the harness with Qwen as its model.","aiUse","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","Engine","Three.js · JavaScript","ai-assisted",[210,211,212,213],{"_51":204,"_26":205,"_18":231},{"_51":193,"_26":194,"_18":189,"_179":195},{"_51":186,"_2